Hello,

On Friday, 2008 May  2 at  1:53:08 +0200, Maximilian Wilhelm wrote:
> Hi!
>=20
> While running some firewalls in somewhat greater networks, I missed
> the possibility to put all netfitler related LOG entries into a
> seperate logfile.

IMHO, you should use NFLOG or ULOG combined with ulogd or ulogd2. It is
easy to have the daemon logging into a separate file. Furthermore, the
performance are far better with the [NF|U]LOG system because it is
possible to use a threshold (via the --nflog-threshold for example).

> How about introducing a new 'firewall' or 'netfilter' syslog facility
> covering all log entries generated by netfilter LOG?

This idea make sense but I don't think it has to be linked with firewall
on big network.

